  "content": "# Unique Vault Code for Station Amber\n\n**LAMINA847263**\n\n---\n\n# Travel Journal: The Ascent to Vellmar\n\n## Day One\n\nThe road to Vellmar began where the paved world ended, near the village of Oakhaven, and I have never driven such a treacherous path in my life. My jeep climbed a winding mountain trail that seemed designed by someone with a personal grudge against my suspension. The air grew thinner and colder with every kilometer, and the forest that had surrounded me gave way to jagged rock faces dusted with early snow. I had come here chasing rumors of an ancient botanical tradition\u2014villagers who claimed to cultivate plants that grew nowhere else on earth. As a botanist, such claims should have made me skeptical, but the old herbarium records I'd studied in university suggested there might be truth to them. I rolled down the window to let in the crisp alpine air, breathing in something I couldn't quite name, a mixture of pine and something wilder, more ancient.\n\n## Day Two\n\nThe storm hit me on the second day, catching me at a pass that offered no shelter. Rain lashed against the windshield in diagonal sheets, and thunder cracked",
